WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:10.648
Before an aircraft is released, a ship remains available, a nuclear change is
accepted or a public decision is defended, someone must

00:10.648 --> 00:13.925
establish what the approved evidence actually says.

00:13.925 --> 00:20.011
Requirements, policies, standards, instructions, revisions and exceptions are
spread across people and departments.

00:20.011 --> 00:28.436
The accountable professional must find the governing source, understand its
context and show how the conclusion was reached.

00:28.436 --> 00:32.649
The outcome may be operational, financial, legal or safety-critical.

00:32.649 --> 00:34.990
The evidence problem comes first.

00:35.990 --> 00:38.899
A search result can locate a page.

00:38.899 --> 00:48.872
It does not establish that the page is current, that a referenced document is
present or that two departments are working from the same

00:48.872 --> 00:49.703
approved revision.

00:49.703 --> 00:54.690
The problem is larger than one query and larger than one workstation.

00:54.690 --> 00:56.768
Engineers need local working context.

00:56.768 --> 00:58.430
Departments need controlled exchange.

00:58.430 --> 01:05.910
Site authorities need visible lineage, scope and disagreement without turning
a central system into an automatic decision maker.

01:06.910 --> 01:11.102
Cortessa is being developed as a site-contained controlled-document
intelligence environment.

01:11.102 --> 01:14.037
Every engineer has a self-sufficient Cortessa box.

01:14.037 --> 01:20.745
Those boxes connect through departmental nodes to an on-site hub, all inside
the site's air-gapped boundary.

01:20.745 --> 01:27.453
The hub is not a central artificial intelligence and it cannot approve on an
engineer's behalf.

01:27.453 --> 01:31.645
It carries only the scope it is enrolled to hold.

01:31.645 --> 01:39.611
The architecture keeps local evidence work close to the engineer while giving
approved revisions a governed route through the

01:39.611 --> 01:40.030
organisation.

01:41.030 --> 01:45.446
Each engineer box holds its approved documents and working context.

01:45.446 --> 01:50.303
Extraction, cleaning, chunking, indexing, retrieval and the resident model run
locally.

01:50.303 --> 01:55.160
Audit and Ask do not depend on a public cloud service.

01:55.160 --> 01:58.251
Retrieval-only operation remains available as the floor.

01:58.251 --> 02:00.017
Author is in development.

02:00.017 --> 02:07.965
Access to documents remains governed by the organisation, and the box does not
silently widen a user's authority.

02:07.965 --> 02:15.030
Local self-sufficiency is what allows the site network to remain sovereign
rather than becoming a dependency.

02:16.030 --> 02:19.245
Audit is the centre of the product.

02:19.245 --> 02:26.595
It reviews the approved corpus for documentary issues worth human attention:
missing references, supersession, revision uncertainty,

02:26.595 --> 02:28.892
terminology, effectivity and structured conflicts.

02:28.892 --> 02:35.782
Each result is a cited candidate for review, not an automatic finding,
approval or certification.

02:35.782 --> 02:44.510
The engineer sees the source route, the document state and the policy
governing what Cortessa is allowed to present.

02:45.510 --> 02:49.549
A candidate becomes useful when its evidence can be challenged.

02:49.549 --> 02:55.204
Cortessa opens the original source passage and preserves the route back to the
document.

02:55.204 --> 03:00.454
The reviewer can inspect surrounding wording, revision and applicability
before forming a judgement.

03:00.454 --> 03:02.474
Ask follows the same discipline.

03:02.474 --> 03:10.956
Answers are tied to cited source spans, and the system can refuse when the
approved corpus does not contain the fact.

03:10.956 --> 03:12.975
Verified indicates provenance, not correctness.

03:12.975 --> 03:18.630
The human decides whether the cited wording answers the question and governs
the work.

03:19.630 --> 03:25.481
The engineer adjudicates the evidence and approves a revision through the
organisation's human process.

03:25.481 --> 03:31.331
The revision is bound to its owner, content digest, parents and permitted
sharing scope.

03:31.331 --> 03:33.003
Its history remains inspectable.

03:33.003 --> 03:39.689
That approved revision can then move to the departmental node and, where
authorised, the on-site hub.

03:39.689 --> 03:42.196
A receiving engineer still reviews it.

03:42.196 --> 03:48.883
Receipt does not silently certify it, make it current or insert it into
another searchable corpus.

03:48.883 --> 03:51.390
Promotion remains a governed human action.

03:52.390 --> 03:57.932
Department scope is checked before a revision is received, queued or exported.

03:57.932 --> 03:59.780
Missing ancestry remains explicit.

03:59.780 --> 04:01.627
Competing branches remain visible.

04:01.627 --> 04:06.246
Arrival time and hub rank do not choose a winner.

04:06.246 --> 04:11.327
The signed offline exchange contract and local integration are implemented
foundations.

04:11.327 --> 04:18.255
Authenticated peer transport, key provisioning, delivery scheduling, backup,
corpus promotion and production rollout remain in

04:18.255 --> 04:18.716
development.

04:18.716 --> 04:27.030
Cortessa is not presented as an already deployed site network or as a
replacement for every records-management function.

04:28.030 --> 04:36.153
In Defence and civil aerospace, Cortessa can support the documentary route
behind maintenance release, engineering change and

04:36.153 --> 04:37.109
airworthiness review.

04:37.109 --> 04:46.188
In nuclear, energy and rail, it can help authorised teams inspect the sources
behind change, asset integrity and engineering

04:46.188 --> 04:46.666
acceptance.

04:46.666 --> 04:56.222
Cortessa does not fly an aircraft, put a ship to sea, approve a nuclear
change, control infrastructure or certify compliance.

04:56.222 --> 05:03.390
It helps the responsible people find, challenge and govern the documentary
evidence behind those outcomes.

05:04.390 --> 05:10.248
A bank can map engineer boxes to policy, risk and assurance teams.

05:10.248 --> 05:16.107
A pharmaceutical site can map them to quality, validation and change control.

05:16.107 --> 05:24.406
Legal and government estates can preserve matter, department and records
boundaries while keeping the source route inspectable.

05:24.406 --> 05:28.312
The vocabulary and authority structure change by sector.

05:28.312 --> 05:36.612
The product discipline does not: local evidence work, cited candidates, human
adjudication, signed revisions and explicitly scoped

05:36.612 --> 05:37.588
internal movement.

05:37.588 --> 05:42.470
No customer deployment, validated use or sector approval is implied.

05:43.470 --> 05:47.466
The credible first step is a bounded evaluation.

05:47.466 --> 05:51.961
Choose one workflow, one cleared corpus and named reviewers.

05:51.961 --> 05:56.956
Agree the baseline and evidence standard before the test begins.

05:56.956 --> 06:01.951
Include difficult scans, tables, ambiguous references and deliberately absent
evidence.

06:01.951 --> 06:06.946
Measure the effort needed to locate and inspect governing sources.

06:06.946 --> 06:12.440
Record accepted and rejected candidates, appropriate refusals, reproducibility
and corpus-preparation effort.

06:12.440 --> 06:22.430
Then use that evidence to define the first departmental workflow, authority
route and controls required for a wider site deployment.

06:23.430 --> 06:31.027
Cortessa begins with a self-sufficient instrument at the engineer's desk and a
simple promise: evidence before authority.

06:31.027 --> 06:33.262
Bring one bounded document workflow.

06:33.262 --> 06:37.284
Test Audit and Ask against evidence standards you control.

06:37.284 --> 06:45.328
Then examine how approved revisions could move through your departments
without leaving the site boundary or surrendering human

06:45.328 --> 06:45.775
authority.

06:45.775 --> 06:49.350
Start a conversation about a scoped Cortessa evaluation.
